        ":question/id": "659f4527-cc88-5c6b-8485-f595eee1689f",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $N(x,y)=\u27e8x{e}^{y},\\sqrt{x+y}\u27e9$\n- **II.** $P(x,y,z)=\u27e8{e}^{x-2y},\\sqrt{3-x},3{z}^{3}\u27e9$\n- **III.** $Q(x,y,z)=\u27e8-1,2,\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2x-y+z)\u27e9$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $N(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $P(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,3-x\\ge 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,2x-y+z>0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
